================ STEP 0: the interpolated quantities ================
anchors LOW 220 / HIGH 1000000   T_MIN -0.5 / T_MAX 1   window width 4 over 8 tiers

0a. peak = windowStart + peakOffset  (SlimeRoll.luau:79, :94)
    peakOffset = lerp(SLIME_PEAK_OFFSET_LOW 1.0000, SLIME_PEAK_OFFSET_HIGH 1.0000, t)
    endpoints are IDENTICAL -> peakOffset is CONSTANT in t
    peak is NOT an index. It is the real-valued CENTRE of the generalised
    Gaussian, in slime-tier units, used only as `dist = i - peak` inside the
    windowStart..windowStart+3 loop (SlimeRoll.luau:98-104). Nothing indexes
    a table with it, so it cannot be out of range; what it can do is move
    the peak outside the window, which would put the modal weight on a tier
    that gets no weight assigned at all.

